:235},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":237,"path":238,"stem":239,"icon":240},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":242,"path":243,"stem":244,"icon":179},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":246,"path":247,"stem":248,"icon":38},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":253},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":255,"path":256,"stem":257,"icon":258},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":260,"path":261,"stem":262,"icon":263},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":265,"title":176,"body":266,"description":590,"extension":591,"links":592,"meta":593,"navigation":594,"path":177,"seo":595,"stem":178,"__hash__":596},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F01.architecture.md",{"type":267,"value":268,"toc":581},"minimark",[269,273,277,281,345,353,357,425,429,432,442,448,453,464,509,515,519,541,574,577],[270,271,31],"h2",{"id":272},"overview",[274,275,276],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[270,278,280],{"id":279},"core-components","Core Components",[282,283,284,301,314,327,333,339],"ul",{},[285,286,287,291,292,296,297,300],"li",{},[288,289,290],"strong",{},"Management server"," (",[293,294,295],"code",{},"kinotic-server-management",") — The API the portal, the Kinotic CLI and organization members' MCP hosts call: sign-up, logins and invitations, the ",[293,298,299],{},"management-api"," services, and the GitHub App's webhook.",[285,302,303,291,306,309,310,313],{},[288,304,305],{},"System server",[293,307,308],{},"kinotic-server-system",") — The API the system console and the vm-managers call: the ",[293,311,312],{},"system-api"," services, project deployments, and the cluster singletons that reconcile deployments and delete old workload runs.",[285,315,316,291,319,322,323,326],{},[288,317,318],{},"App server",[293,320,321],{},"kinotic-server-app",") — The API every application's users, UIs and microservices call: the ",[293,324,325],{},"app-api"," persistence services and the services applications publish in their own zones, each application at its own API host.",[285,328,329,332],{},[288,330,331],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Each server's gateway routes remote procedure calls between its clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket, and serves the server's REST and MCP endpoints.",[285,334,335,338],{},[288,336,337],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[285,340,341,344],{},[288,342,343],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC) across three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application. Each server admits only the participants it serves.",[274,346,347,348,352],{},"The three servers are Spring Boot applications that form one Ignite cluster, in which each hosts only its own zones. ",[349,350,199],"a",{"href":351},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth#network-architecture"," shows which participants each admits and which zones each hosts.",[270,354,356],{"id":355},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[358,359,360,373],"table",{},[361,362,363],"thead",{},[364,365,366,370],"tr",{},[367,368,369],"th",{},"Component",[367,371,372],{},"Technology",[374,375,376,385,393,401,409,417],"tbody",{},[364,377,378,382],{},[379,380,381],"td",{},"Orchestration",[379,383,384],{},"Kubernetes",[364,386,387,390],{},[379,388,389],{},"Build Isolation",[379,391,392],{},"Firecracker VMs",[364,394,395,398],{},[379,396,397],{},"Runtime",[379,399,400],{},"Bun",[364,402,403,406],{},[379,404,405],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[379,407,408],{},"Elasticsearch",[364,410,411,414],{},[379,412,413],{},"Logging",[379,415,416],{},"Grafana Loki",[364,418,419,422],{},[379,420,421],{},"Payments",[379,423,424],{},"Stripe Connect",[270,426,428],{"id":427},"communication","Communication",[274,430,431],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[433,434,439],"pre",{"className":435,"code":437,"language":438},[436],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[293,440,437],{"__ignoreMap":441},"",[274,443,444,445,447],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[349,446,232],{"href":233}," reference for details.",[449,450,452],"h3",{"id":451},"kinotic-rpc-on-its-own","Kinotic RPC on its own",[274,454,455,456,459,460,463],{},"Kinotic RPC, the service and event layer in ",[293,457,458],{},"kinotic-core"," and ",[293,461,462],{},"kinotic-api-gateway",", runs without the rest of\nKinotic OS. A server built on it alone supplies two beans the gateway authenticates and authorizes every\nconnection with:",[358,465,466,476],{},[361,467,468],{},[364,469,470,473],{},[367,471,472],{},"Bean",[367,474,475],{},"What it decides",[374,477,478,491],{},[364,479,480,485],{},[379,481,482],{},[293,483,484],{},"SecurityService",[379,486,487,488],{},"Who a connection is: it authenticates the STOMP CONNECT headers and returns the connection's ",[293,489,490],{},"Participant",[364,492,493,498],{},[379,494,495],{},[293,496,497],{},"ZoneRulesResolver",[379,499,500,501,504,505,508],{},"What that participant may address: the ",[293,502,503],{},"ZoneRules"," of zones it may send to and subscribe in, which the gateway narrows to the zones the server's ",[293,506,507],{},"ZonePartitioningService"," serves",[274,510,511,512,514],{},"Kinotic OS's servers supply each from their own module: the ",[293,513,484],{}," of the server, and kinotic-domain's\nresolver, which gives system, organization and application participants their zones.",[449,516,518],{"id":517},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[274,520,521,522,525,526,529,530,529,533,536,537,540],{},"A Java service published with ",[293,523,524],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[293,527,528],{},"Future",", ",[293,531,532],{},"CompletableFuture",[293,534,535],{},"Mono"," or ",[293,538,539],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[433,542,546],{"className":543,"code":544,"language":545,"meta":441,"style":441},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[293,547,548,556,562,568],{"__ignoreMap":441},[549,550,553],"span",{"class":551,"line":552},"line",1,[549,554,555],{},"@Override\n",[549,557,559],{"class":551,"line":558},2,[549,560,561],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[549,563,565],{"class":551,"line":564},3,[549,566,567],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[549,569,571],{"class":551,"line":570},4,[549,572,573],{},"}\n",[274,575,576],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[578,579,580],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":441,"searchDepth":558,"depth":558,"links":582},[583,584,585,586],{"id":272,"depth":558,"text":31},{"id":279,"depth":558,"text":280},{"id":355,"depth":558,"text":356},{"id":427,"depth":558,"text":428,"children":587},[588,589],{"id":451,"depth":564,"text":452},{"id":517,"depth":564,"text":518},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":179},{"title":176,"description":590},"ggXFHW1jM4SzoVJQNjkBWucJSO-WTGMjCfB23F0MG90",[598,600],{"title":167,"path":168,"stem":169,"description":599,"icon":90,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":181,"path":182,"stem":183,"description":601,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1793011040650]